Z||000000||Alex4mula||03-13-2001||08:25 AM||||I was looking at the Evolution 4 car cover that Fiero Store sales for $160. Looks pretty good but...  does someone knows a place to get it cheaper? Any other cover of same or better quality for our car? I just painted my car & want a good outdoor cover to protect it while parked at work. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||03-13-2001||09:02 AM||||I bought a Budge medium size from Auto Zone a year ago for around $20 to $40, and it fits great. ||||reg||6
Z||000002||deceler8||03-13-2001||09:19 AM||||Get a Sportsman's Guide catalog or go to <A HREF="http://www.sportsmansguide.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sportsmansguide.com</A>  and order a surplus parachute. I picked one up for $15 a while back and I cover my antique truck with it. <P>This thing will outlast any car cover and it's soft and light. But I do park the truck indoors...you will want a contoured cover if you park outdoors.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||03-13-2001||09:23 AM||||I need sun UV protection and definetly has to be for outdoor (i.e wet). Fit is not that important as long as it stays on on windy days.||||reg||1
